From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: list the 10-bit profiles in the default profile
 list

When the driver has no profile control, V4L2Device::queryC2Profiles()
falls back to a built-in list. The iris gen1 decoder has none (its
capability table only has PIPE and STAGE), and the list only has 8-bit
profiles, so HEVC Main 10 and VP9 Profile 2 are missing from
MediaCodecList. Players that choose a decoder from these capabilities,
such as mpv, decode 10-bit streams in software; ExoPlayer reports the
format as unsupported but still tries the hardware decoder.

Add PROFILE_VP9_2 and PROFILE_HEVC_MAIN_10. The similar list in
DecodeInterface.cpp is only used when this one is empty.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needs 10-bit decoding in the driver, patches/kernel/iris/0012]
---
 v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp b/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
index d72219a..eab8d61 100644
--- a/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
@@ -1756,7 +1756,7 @@ std::vector<C2Config::profile_t> V4L2Device::queryC2Profiles(uint32_t pixFmt) {
     case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME:
         if (!getSupportedProfiles(VideoCodec::VP9, &profiles)) {
             ALOGW("Driver doesn't support QUERY VP9 profiles, use default values, Profile0");
-            profiles = {C2Config::PROFILE_VP9_0};
+            profiles = {C2Config::PROFILE_VP9_0, C2Config::PROFILE_VP9_2};
         }
         break;
     case V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC:
@@ -1766,6 +1766,7 @@ std::vector<C2Config::profile_t> V4L2Device::queryC2Profiles(uint32_t pixFmt) {
                   "use default values, Main");
             profiles = {
                     C2Config::PROFILE_HEVC_MAIN,
+                    C2Config::PROFILE_HEVC_MAIN_10,
             };
         }
         break;
